*.local

# Environment
# `.env` holds real secrets, including the admin password, and used to be
# committed. Keep it local. A fresh checkout needs SUPABASE_URL,
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY and their VITE_ twins to build.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Package manager
# `bun.lock` is deliberately untracked. CI installs with npm, so
# `package-lock.json` is the lockfile a build actually reads. A tracked `bun.lock`
# that no build consults can still conflict on every merge and drift silently from
# `package.json` - which is exactly how main's CI broke, when a tool bumped the
# dependency in `package.json` and only this file. `bunfig.toml` stays: its 24h
# `minimumReleaseAge` guard still applies to anyone who runs bun locally, though
# note that npm does not honour it.
bun.lock

# Wrangler / Cloudflare
.wrangler/
.dev.vars

# Supabase CLI scratch state (`supabase link`, `db push`).
# Holds the linked project ref, the pooler URL and cached service versions. Machine-local:
# committing it would pin one developer's linked project into the repository.
supabase/.temp/

# Created by running the local stack (`npx supabase start`). Holds only `_current_branch`,
# but it is machine-local scratch state like the above, not a source file.
supabase/.branches/

# Local benchmark output (`npm run bench:scheduling` writes its report here)
.benchmark/

# Impeccable design skill: per-task scratch output and the launcher's self-downloaded
# binaries. The skill text, hook configuration and `.impeccable/design.json` are source.
.impeccable/build/
.impeccable/review/
.impeccable/mocks/
.impeccable/decision/
.impeccable/surfaces/
.impeccable/questions/
**/skills/impeccable/scripts/bin/

